course: dictionary
lesson: 9588
title: One word, many streets
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A street is a road in a town or city, with houses, shops or buildings along its sides. You meet the word in addresses too: «24 High Street» tells you the house is on a road called High Street.
explain: The word can also mean the town outside, and the people in it. «The streets» can mean all the people out there. Look at the words around it to decide which meaning fits. Is the sentence about a road, a name, or people?
explain: Maths and safety use the word in real ways. Houses on a street can be counted, and lamps along a street stand at equal gaps. When you cross a street, look both ways first. A street name on a map helps you find your way.
fact: A street is a road in a town or city, with houses, shops or buildings on its sides.
fact: «Street» is part of many addresses, such as «24 High Street».
fact: «The streets» can mean the town outside and the people in it.
fact: Phrases you may meet include «cross the street», «down the street», «across the street», «main street» and «high street».
fact: A high street, in the UK, is a main road with lots of shops on it.
exercise: What is a street? | A river that runs through a town | A long field with a fence round it | A tunnel under a hill | *A road in a town or city with houses, shops or buildings on its sides
exercise: «A boy in California crossed a street while looking at his phone.» What does crossing the street mean? | *Walking from one side of the road to the other | Driving a car down the road | Sitting on a bench in the park
exercise: Which word in the address «24 High Street» tells you it is a road? | 24 | *Street | High
test: «Lamps stood along the street at equal gaps.» What does the word street mean here? | The people who live in the town | A shop with a big window | *A road in a town or city
test: «The streets buzzed with talk about the new park.» What do the streets mean? | *The town outside and the people in it | Houses numbered on one side only | Only the road surfaces
exam: «For a while the street looked at Jamie differently.» What does the street mean here? | *The people living on the street | Only the road surface | The car that hit him | A shop on the high street
